    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping per-city sequence numbers entirely, and moved every value derived from the code onto the new identity.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 Rewrote to produce `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n- `REGION` = region derived from the postcode via `Locality.of(city, postcode)` (postcode-first, matching the spec and the existing region model).\n- `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (the telephone is already E.164-normalized upstream by `NormalizeTelephone`, so the stored value is used directly).\n- Removed the `OwnerRepository` dependency and the per-city count/sequence \u2014 no longer needed.\n\n**`Locality.java`** \u2014 Added `ofCustomerCode(customerCode)`, which reads the locality back off the identity by taking the `REGION` segment before the first `-` (returns `UNKNOWN` when absent). This is how the locality derivation \"moves to\" the new identity rather than being computed independently.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Repointed the `locality` mapping from `Locality.of(city, postcode)` to `Locality.ofCustomerCode(customerCode)`, so locality flows from the same region-and-hash identity.\n\n**Values that already flowed through `customerCode` automatically pick up the new identity** (verified, with Javadoc updated to match):\n- **Membership number** (`AssignMembershipNumber`) \u2014 still `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, now over the new code (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26`).\n- **Check digit** (`CheckDigit` / mapper) \u2014 Luhn over the decimal digits of the code; the hex letters `A-F` and the dash are ignored, so it now covers the digits within `<REGION>-<HASH8>`.\n- **Create audit record** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 logs the new `customerCode` (visible in the run: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n**Tests:** the new `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
